  "id": "DrugBank_DB00997 - MONDO_6335",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Doxorubicin is linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma via two distinct but related mechanisms. First, Doxorubicin is associated with Malignant Germ Cell Tumor of Ovary, which in turn is linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma. Second, Doxorubicin is also connected to Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma, which is further linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma via Carboplatin. These pathways highlight a potential role for Doxorubicin in the development of this cancer, possibly through its antitumor effects or by influencing cellular processes that contribute to tumor progression. The overlapping indications and the shared downstream targets suggest a possible mechanism of action that involves either direct cytotoxic effects or indirect regulatory influences on tumor biology. The evidence supports a relationship between Doxorubicin and Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
